course: dictionary
lesson: 1576
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one you need. «He has lots of charm» means the power to please people. A charm bracelet means a bracelet with small ornaments on it. Read the clues before you choose a meaning.
explain: Charm can also be a verb, a doing word. To charm someone is to please or attract them. In the phrase «work like a charm», charm is a noun meaning a special power, and the phrase means it works very well. Ask yourself: what word would fit here?
explain: The Rat says that «Nothing seems really to matter, that's the charm of it.» Here charm means the attractive quality that makes something pleasing, even when things go wrong. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Charm has several meanings: the power to please people, a small ornament, an object believed to bring luck, and a verb meaning to please or attract someone.
fact: A «lucky charm» is an object that people believe will bring good luck.
fact: «Work like a charm» means work very well.
fact: «Turn on the charm» means to try hard to please someone.
fact: «Rizz» is young people's slang for charm, and Oxford chose it as its Word of the Year for 2023.
exercise: «He has lots of charm, and everyone wants to be his friend.» What does charm mean here? | *The power to please and attract people | A tune played on a flute | A small ornament on a bracelet | Something that makes you cough
exercise: Mia's bracelet has a tiny silver horseshoe on it. What is the horseshoe called? | A horse | *A charm | A coin | A bracelet
exercise: Which phrase means to try hard to please someone? | Lucky charm | *Turn on the charm | Work like a charm | Charm bracelet
test: Ben says a charm is always a piece of jewellery. Is he right? | Yes, but only on bracelets | No, charms only appear in stories | *No, a charm can be an object or words believed to bring good luck | Yes, a charm is always jewellery
test: «Nothing seems really to matter, that's the charm of it.» What does charm mean in this sentence? | An object believed to bring good luck | A small ornament on a bracelet | To control someone by magic | *The attractive quality that makes something pleasing
exam: «Rizz» means charm in slang, and it became Oxford's Word of the Year for 2023. Why can some slang end up in a dictionary? | Dictionaries only add words from old books | Parents write all the dictionaries | *Some slang settles down and is used for a long time | Slang is always banned from dictionaries
